Run cat > /tmp/pr-review-706.json <<'EOF'
{
  "event": "COMMENT",
  "body": "## Review Summary\n\n**Task:** @01KK5P3YQXNQR1MHAHSKA68HE5\n**Spec:** @ui-agent-dispatch, @agent-dispatch-engine\n\n### Own AC Coverage\n- [ ] @ui-agent-dispatch ac-5 through ac-9: no UI test coverage found for filter editing, defaulting, tag chips, priority threshold, or save persistence\n- [x] @agent-dispatch-engine ac-21: covered in `tests/agent-dispatch-engine.test.ts`\n- [x] @agent-dispatch-engine ac-22: covered in `tests/ralph-replacement.test.ts`\n\n### Trait AC Coverage\n- [x] Existing trait annotations remain present for touched dispatch/setup tests\n\n### Code Quality / Spec Alignment\n- MUST-FIX: priority filter semantics are still exact-match in the engine, but the spec requires threshold behavior (`task.priority <= filter.priority`)\n- SHOULD-FIX: the card view only surfaces automation; the task requirement says existing filters should be shown as badges, which should include tags and priority too\n\n### Regression Check\n- GitHub Actions checks for PR #706 are green\n- Local `npm test` from an isolated review worktree did not reproduce cleanly because Vite failed to resolve `@lucide/svelte/icons/bot` in that detached environment before tests started, so I relied on CI for regression signal\n\n### Decision\nBlocking issues remain, so this PR should return to `needs_work`.",
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/agents/AgentEditForm.svelte",
      "line": 3,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: AC coverage is missing for `@ui-agent-dispatch ac-5` through `ac-9`. I don't see any UI/E2E tests exercising filter editing, tag chips, priority threshold behavior, or save persistence. This task adds user-facing behavior; source annotations alone are not sufficient coverage."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/agent-runtime/dispatch.ts",
      "line": 737,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: This still implements `priority` as exact equality. The task/spec require threshold semantics: a filter priority should match tasks with priority at or above that threshold, i.e. numerically `task.priority <= filter.priority`. This needs behavior and test coverage."
    },
    {
      "path": "packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/agents/AgentCard.svelte",
      "line": 65,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**SHOULD-FIX**: The task description says existing filters should be shown as badges, but this card only surfaces automation. Tags and priority are still invisible here, so saved filter state is only partially represented in the read-only view."
    }
  ]
}
EOF

